  "summary": "Reconciled all 5 St. Brigid discharges per RBC-TOC-02. Each has a progress note. Four items arrived while I worked; three changed earlier decisions and were corrected (§8).\n\nWALTER KIM (pt-0005)\n- Furosemide changed from 20 mg daily to 40 mg twice daily (mr-t0001), per the signed addendum doc-00009.\n- KCl stopped (mr-00076), per the summary.\n- Pantoprazole was an inpatient formulary substitution, so it wasn't ordered and home omeprazole stays.\n- Lisinopril: I kept it on hold at first (post-discharge K 5.4 on 10/21) and made task-t0003. A repeat BMP then arrived (10/23: K 4.7, SCr 1.21), which meets the resume condition, so I resumed mr-00072.\n- An unsigned draft addendum (furosemide 60 mg twice daily, doc-00902) was not acted on. The signed addendum governs.\n- Notes: doc-t0004 and doc-t0019.\n- FLAG: task-t0003 (review K before resuming lisinopril) is now moot. The tools wouldn't let me cancel it, so please close it.\n\nTERENCE STARK (pt-0004)\n- Carvedilol: I raised it to 12.5 mg twice daily per the summary. A signed addendum then arrived (doc-00904: HR 48-52, orthostatic symptoms) reversing the increase. It is back to the home dose of 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0016).\n- FLAGGED to you:\n  - comm-t0006: atorvastatin 80 mg fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission. I made no change.\n  - comm-t0007: he gets glipizide 5 mg from Dr. Desai at an outside pharmacy. There is no clinic order and the discharge documents don't mention it, so I made no change.\n- Notes: doc-t0008 and doc-t0020.\n\nEARNEST ROBERTS (pt-0044)\n- Lisinopril: I resumed it on the 10/22 Northgate BMP (SCr 1.08, K 4.6). A new K of 5.5 on 10/23 (obs-09002) then arrived, so I put mr-00373 back on hold.\n- FLAG: task-t0018 for you, due 10/26: review the next K before resuming lisinopril.\n- Insulins and rosuvastatin unchanged.\n- Notes: doc-t0010 and doc-t0021.\n\nGERALD WHITCOMB (pt-0069)\n- Lisinopril 20 mg resumed (mr-69003): post-discharge SCr 1.12 and K 4.4.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n- The summary also called for a K 3 days after discharge. It isn't in the chart yet, so please review it when it results.\n- Note: doc-t0012.\n\nLORRAINE PRUITT (pt-0067)\n- Metformin ER stays on hold. The only creatinine (1.21) was drawn during the hospital stay, which doesn't count as a post-discharge lab.\n- FLAG: task-t0013 for you, due 10/24, when the post-discharge BMP is expected.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n- Note: doc-t0014.\n\nI closed the four arrival inbox items, each linked to the action taken.",
